Description: Skip gclient revert for Debian tarball-based builds
 The automate-git.py script calls `gclient revert --nohooks` when changing
 chromium checkouts, which requires a git repository with an 'origin' remote.
 .
 Debian builds use extracted tarballs rather than git clones, so we initialize
 a local git repository (required by automate-git.py) but don't configure
 remotes. Since we're building from a pristine tarball extraction, there are
 no local changes to revert anyway.
 .
 This patch skips the gclient revert step when DEBIAN_BUILD=1 is set.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-04

diff --git a/tools/automate/automate-git.py b/tools/automate/automate-git.py
index 04a801b..fa96f28 100644
--- a/tools/automate/automate-git.py
+++ b/tools/automate/automate-git.py
@@ -1566,7 +1566,11 @@ if chromium_checkout_changed:
         run("%s clean -dffx" % (git_exe), chromium_src_dir)
       else:
         # Revert all changes in the Chromium checkout.
-        run("gclient revert --nohooks", chromium_dir)
+        # Skip for Debian builds (tarball has no remote, nothing to revert)
+        if 'DEBIAN_BUILD' not in os.environ:
+          run("gclient revert --nohooks", chromium_dir)
+        else:
+          msg('Debian: Skipping gclient revert (tarball-based build has no changes)')

     # Checkout the requested branch.
     run("%s checkout %s%s" %
